Subject: [PATCH] book ch.17 extras: regression and smoothing splines, loess
 (p. 460)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- core/stats/smoothing.py: smooth_curve —
  - bspline: regression B-spline (degree 1–3, interior knots at quantiles
    of x) fitted as a multiple regression: SEs and CI band, F test of the
    spline against a straight line, adjusted R², AIC, SBC, lack of fit;
  - smoothing_spline: cubic smoothing spline as penalized B-spline
    regression with knots at the data (the criterion of scipy
    make_smoothing_spline), λ by GCV, effective df = tr S, σ̂² and
    pointwise SEs from the smoother; replicated x handled by weights;
  - loess: statsmodels lowess with robustness iterations (descriptive).
- Tests: B-spline fit equals patsy bs; cubic data reproduced exactly;
  GCV curve equals scipy make_smoothing_spline(lam=None), fixed-λ curve
  equals scipy exactly; λ limits (line, interpolation); loess
  reproduces a line and resists an outlier.

